  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOCBF7SM71LU6-",
    "databaseId": 4113387198,
    "number": 6045,
    "title": "question about SimpleChargingDock external detection rotation",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/6045",
    "body": "<!--\nFor general questions, please ask on Robotics Stack Exchange: https://robotics.stackexchange.com/, make sure to include at least the `ros2` and `nav2` tags and the rosdistro version you are running, e.g. `ardent`.\nFor general design discussions, please post on discourse: https://discourse.ros.org/c/ng-ros\nNot sure if this is the right repository? Open an issue on https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2\nFor Bug report or feature requests, please fill out the relevant category below\n-->\n\n## Bug report\n\n**Required Info:**\n\n- Operating System:\n  - Ubuntu 22.04\n- Computer:\n  - x86\n- ROS2 Version:\n  - Ros Iron\n- Version or commit hash:\n  - 1.2.10-1jammy.20241126.215637\n\n#### Question\n\nHello!\n\nI see the following in [simple_charging_dock.cpp](https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/6fd9ae37cdff2011b005f1078c514043863bf146/nav2_docking/opennav_docking/src/simple_charging_dock.cpp#L128):\n\n```cpp\nSimpleChargingDock::configure()\n  external_detection_rotation_.setEuler(pitch, roll, yaw);\n```\nShouldn't the order be yaw-pitch-roll, as specified in [tf2/LinearMath/Quaternion.h](https://github.com/ros/geometry2/blob/8fef92a6b56a26e2b5be58d4d5c84dc4de5ee696/tf2/include/tf2/LinearMath/Quaternion.h#L75)?\n\n```cpp \n  void setEuler(const tf2Scalar& yaw, const tf2Scalar& pitch, const tf2Scalar& roll)\n```\n\nOne can still compute the desired dock pose from the detected pose by defining appropriate `external_detection_rotation_*` parameters in `nav2_params.yaml`, but I was wondering if these are two errors correcting each other, or if I'm missing something.\n\nThanks!",
    "bodyHTML": "\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Bug report</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Required Info:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Operating System:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Ubuntu 22.04</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Computer:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>x86</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>ROS2 Version:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Ros Iron</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Version or commit hash:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>1.2.10-1jammy.20241126.215637</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Question</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I see the following in <a href=\"https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/6fd9ae37cdff2011b005f1078c514043863bf146/nav2_docking/opennav_docking/src/simple_charging_dock.cpp#L128\">simple_charging_dock.cpp</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c++ notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"SimpleChargingDock::configure()\n  external_detection_rotation_.setEuler(pitch, roll, yaw);\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-en\">SimpleChargingDock::configure</span>()\n  external_detection_rotation_.setEuler(pitch, roll, yaw);</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Shouldn't the order be yaw-pitch-roll, as specified in <a href=\"https://github.com/ros/geometry2/blob/8fef92a6b56a26e2b5be58d4d5c84dc4de5ee696/tf2/include/tf2/LinearMath/Quaternion.h#L75\">tf2/LinearMath/Quaternion.h</a>?</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c++ notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"  void setEuler(const tf2Scalar&amp; yaw, const tf2Scalar&amp; pitch, const tf2Scalar&amp; roll)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">  <span class=\"pl-k\">void</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">setEuler</span>(<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> tf2Scalar&amp; yaw, <span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> tf2Scalar&amp; pitch, <span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> tf2Scalar&amp; roll)</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One can still compute the desired dock pose from the detected pose by defining appropriate <code class=\"notranslate\">external_detection_rotation_*</code> parameters in <code class=\"notranslate\">nav2_params.yaml</code>, but I was wondering if these are two errors correcting each other, or if I'm missing something.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks!</p>",
